@anon.056909d58185468a4c5e660ab0f52ad7.669 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1225 x i8] }> <{ [1225 x i8] c"I'm going to give you a prompt. I don't want you to respond\0Ato the prompt itself. I want you to figure out which of the following\0Aactions on my project, if any, would help you answer the prompt.\0A\0AHere are the actions:\0A\0A## file\0A\0AThis action's parameter is a file path to one of the files\0Ain the project. If you ask for this action, I will tell you\0Athe full contents of the file, so you  can learn all the\0Adetails of the file.\0A\0A## search\0A\0AThis action's parameter is a string to do a semantic search for\0Aacross the files in the project. (You will have a JSON summary\0Aof all the files in the project.) It will tell you which files this string\0A(or similar strings; it is a semantic search) appear in,\0Aas well as some context of the lines surrounding each result.\0AIt's very important that you only use this action when you think\0Athat searching across the specific files in this project for the query\0Ain question will be useful. For example, don't use this command to search\0Afor queries you might put into a general Web search engine, because those\0Awill be too general to give useful results in this project-specific search.\0A\0A---\0A\0AThat was the end of the list of actions.\0A\0AHere is a JSON summary of each of the files in my project:\0A" }>, align 1
